{tab==='market'&&<>{!mobile&&holdings}<div className="sectiontitle">GLOBAL AI HARDWARE MARKET <span>SIMULATED MONTHLY PRICES · USD</span></div><div className="market">{ASSETS.map(asset=>{const owned=s.positions[asset.id]?.qty||0;const change=(s.prices[asset.id]/asset.base-1)*100;return <button key={asset.id} className={'asset '+(selected===asset.id?'chosen':'')} onClick={()=>{setSelected(asset.id);setQty(1);setTradeOpen(true);}}><span className="maker">{asset.maker} <small>{asset.region}</small></span><b>{asset.name}</b><span className="price">{money(s.prices[asset.id])}</span><span className="sub">{asset.kind} · owned {owned}</span><span className={change>=0?'up':'down'}>{change>=0?'+':''}{change.toFixed(1)}% vs start</span></button>;})}</div>{mobile&&holdings}{mobile&&wire}<section className="trade"><div><div className="eyebrow">SELECTED ASSET</div><h2>{a.maker} {a.name}</h2><p>{a.description}</p><div className="mini">Price: <b>{money(p)}</b> · You own: <b>{held.qty}</b> · Avg. paid: <b>{held.qty?money(held.cost/held.qty):'—'}</b></div></div><div className="tradecontrols"><label htmlFor="quantity">QUANTITY</label><input id="quantity" type="number" min="1" max="999" value={qty} onChange={e=>setQty(Number(e.target.value))}/><div className="actions"><button className="buy" disabled={!canTrade||!!s.threat||s.cash<buyTotal} onClick={()=>trade('buy')}>BUY · {short(buyTotal)}</button><button className="sell" disabled={!canTrade||!!s.threat||held.qty<count} onClick={()=>trade('sell')}>SELL · {short(sellTotal)}</button></div><small>{held.qty>=count?`Selling now: ${sellProfit>=0?'+':''}${money(sellProfit)} realized ${sellProfit>=0?'profit':'loss'} (fees included)`:`Buy includes 1% fee. You need ${count} owned to sell.`}</small></div></section></>}
{tab==='lab'&&<section className="lab"><div className="eyebrow">RECURRING BUSINESS</div><h2>YOUR AI LAB · LEVEL {s.labs}</h2><p>Build capacity, win inference contracts and generate predictable revenue. One upgrade increases both income and operating expenses.</p><div className="labgrid"><div><small>MONTHLY REVENUE</small><b>{money(monthlyRevenue(s.labs))}</b></div><div><small>MONTHLY OPERATING COST</small><b>{money(monthlyExpenses(s.labs))}</b></div><div><small>MONTHLY PROFIT</small><b className="green">{money(monthlyProfit(s.labs))}</b></div><div><small>ANNUAL REVENUE RUN RATE</small><b>{money(monthlyRevenue(s.labs)*12)}</b></div></div><div className="upgrade"><div><b>NEXT LAB UPGRADE</b><p>Costs {money(labCost(s.labs))} · Adds +$420,000 revenue/month, −$150,000 expenses/month, <strong>+$270,000 profit/month</strong>.</p><small>Simple payback: {(labCost(s.labs)/270000).toFixed(1)} months. Income starts on the next month.</small></div><button disabled={s.ended||!!s.threat||!!s.crisisResult||s.month<4||s.labs>=8||s.cash<labCost(s.labs)} onClick={upgrade}>{s.month<4?'UNLOCKS MONTH 4':s.labs>=8?'MAX LEVEL':s.cash<labCost(s.labs)?'NOT ENOUGH CASH':'UPGRADE LAB'}</button></div></section>}
{tab==='rules'&&<section className="rules tutorial"><div className="eyebrow">WELCOME TO SILICON HUSTLE</div><h2>THREE MOVES. ONE $100M EXIT.</h2><div className="steps"><div><b>01 · BUY</b><p>Pick a real AI accelerator, like the NVIDIA H100. Buy units with your $5M cash.</p></div><div><b>02 · NEXT MONTH</b><p>Move time forward. Prices change. Hold what you bought or look for another deal.</p></div><div><b>03 · SELL</b><p>Sell above your purchase price to make money. Your trade shows profit after fees.</p></div></div><p className="tutorialgoal"><b>YOUR GOAL:</b> Reach $100M in 30 months. Make it, and you can cash out or risk everything for something bigger.</p><button className="starttrade" onClick={startTrading}>START BUILDING →</button><details className="more-rules"><summary>More about winning, losing, and pricing</summary><p><b>WIN:</b> Reach $100M valuation by Month 30 to unlock fictional acquisition offers. IPO is a rare bonus at $150M valuation, $12M annual revenue run rate and positive operating profit. These are game rules, not actual exchange listing criteria.</p><p><b>LOSE:</b> Miss the target and receive a satirical business-magazine headline. Run out of cash and shut down. Every four months, investors may challenge your leadership. Respond to activist investors, takeover attempts, and shareholder votes. At Month 30, you receive your result and any exit choices. Losing founders receive a dynamic final cover. No prison for ordinary business failure.</p><p className="fine">Hardware values are approximate 2026 market reference points, not live executable quotes. Some accelerators are sold in integrated servers, not individually. Game trading treats them as standardized per-accelerator economic units for playability. Cerebras WSE-3, Groq LPU, Etched Sohu and cloud-only accelerators are excluded from spot trading until realistic unit economics can be modeled.</p></details></section>}
